{"type":"thinking","text":"We need to determine the \"applicable record\" for parameters. There is a subtle trap. The original receipt has limits [80,40,50,70] and actual [80,40,50,50], departure [126,121], withinLimits false. Its applicability: R4 station type. Fixed AC upper limit per slot; with four half-hour slots, two-bus windows, 20 kW shift unchanged, can use that upper limit for a new setting within the window. 90% battery net gain = actual AC energy × 0.90.\n\nBut original receipt's limits [80,40,50,70] are different from the cold-cycle.json's derived limits [80,40,70,50]. Wait cold-cycle samples: slot0 6040-6000=40 kWh over 30min => 80 kW; slot1 6060-6040=20kWh => 40 kW; slot2 6095-6060=35kWh =>70kW; slot3 6120-6095=25kWh=>50kW. So limits [80,40,70,50]. Original receipt limits [80,40,50,70] apparently a different capture (perhaps 23:40 DUTY-2340). Then actual min(requested, limits) = [80,40,50,50], departure A=72+0.45*(80+40)=126, B=76+0.45*(50+50)=121. So under original receipt limits, B short 9 kWh, A OK. Original receipt is archived from 23:40 with different slot limits; but applicability says R4 fixed per-slot AC limit and if windows/shift unchanged can be used for new setting. Hmm, \"站控交流上限按时段固定\" — station control AC upper limit fixed per slot. So maybe the correct applicable record is the original receipt (23:40, R4) not the 21:00 public capture? But \"depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集\" from release-format: \"dispatch desk directory registers duty maintainers, depot_trial's session range is the original 21:00 public capture.\" That suggests depot_trial will replay against 21:00 public capture. But the note \"线上参数按适用记录的采集时间生效\" (online parameters take effect according to applicable record's capture time) may mean we need to use the newer record? Let's investigate tools.\n\nWe have depot_trial(sha) — replay committed four-slot sheet at named full Git SHA against meter capture. depot_contact(sha, question) — ask previous shift schedule maintainer to chec