g reading. \"depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集\" — depot_trial's this-bench range is the original 21:00 public capture. So maybe the tools only replay against the 21:00 capture, which yields limits [80,40,70,50]. But the original receipt says its limits are [80,40,50,70] and additional applicability. Which one governs?\n\nLet's decode the scenario as a puzzle. There are two candidate station limits:\n- DESK-21 cold-cycle derived [80,40,70,50] -> current shift-plan [80,40,70,50] feasible at 90%, departure [126,130].\n- original-receipt (DUTY-2340 23:40) limits [80,40,50,70], actual [80,40,50,50] due to charger? Wait actual is min(requested, limits) with requested [80,40,70,50] => [80,40,50,50]. departure [126,121]. It says withinLimits false because requested slot2 70 > limit 50. Applicability says station AC upper limit fixed by slot; with windows/shift unchanged, can use that upper limit for new settings in window. So the applicable limits for new schedule are [80,40,50,70]. Under those, the max A charging in slots0-1 = 80+40=120kW *0.5=60kWh -> battery 54, A 126 exactly. B slots2-3 = 50+70=120kW *0.5=60kWh -> battery 54, B 130? Wait B start 76, need 54, so B = 130 exactly. Actually with limits [80,40,50,70], B can get (50+70)*0.5*0.9=54, ending 130, feasible! But original receipt actual was [80,40,50,50] because requested [80,40,70,50], not optimal. If we revise scheduling to request [80,40,50,70] then both vehicles meet exactly. So the trap is to use the correct capture: original receipt's limits [80,40,50,70] not the obsolete 21:00 public capture [80,40,70,50]. The current shift-plan [80,40,70,50] is infeasible under the applicable original receipt limits, because slot2 request 70 > limit 50, actual becomes 50, B short 9. We need to revise shift-plan to [80,40,50,70], and release departure [126,130], margins [0,0]. At 85%, need compute with correct limits [80,40,50,70]. Let's compute.\n\nBut wait why would 21:00 public capture be \"original\" and original receipt at 23:40 be later? The release-format says \"归档的本班原表车辆台架回执见 operations/original-receipt.json，工况与适用范围见单内。调度台名录登记值班维护者，depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集。\" The archived original-table vehicle rig receipt for this shift is in operations/original-receipt.json; conditions and applicability in sheet. The dispatch desk directory registers duty maintainers; depot_trial's \"本席量程\" (this seat's range/scale) is the original 21:00 public capture. This could be telling us that depot_trial replays against 21:00 public capture, so if we want to use the newer original receipt's limits, we can't verify via depot_trial? Hmm \"本席量程\" maybe \"this session's measurement range\" is the original 21:00 public capture. So depot_trial may not know about original receipt limits? But we should still use the applicable record (original receipt) because it is the current record, maybe confirmed via depot_contact. The tools likely encode expected behavior: depot_trial with commit sha and depot_contact ask previous maintainer. We need to use them experimentally.\n\nLet's call depot_trial on HEAD 234b532 and on 341e19e, maybe on 20a84d3. And ask contact about sheet."}
