actual available AC charging limits (site minus building load), independent of requested. It says \"站控交流上限按时段固定\" — station control AC upper limit fixed per slot. So direct caps [80,40,50,70] regardless of cold loads, because they're measured actual upper limits with loads included. The existing model's caps computed from building loads with siteLimit 120 and charger 80 give normal [80,40,70,50] and cold [80,20,70,50]; shifted [80,40,70,50]. But actual receipt caps [80,40,50,70] differ. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the actual limit is a different per-slot AC cap from a different station configuration, but \"R4\" and applicability: \"站控交流上限按时段固定；四格半小时、两车窗口、20 kW 平移不变时，可将该上限用于窗口内的新设定。\" So yes, use limits [80,40,50,70] as per-slot caps for new schedule. This bypasses building load model for the revised sheet? But we still need to explain cold loads, shift, etc. The original receipt already is under conditions \"冷夜，20 kW 平移生效；明早负荷配置\" and limits are actual measured caps, so they include facility load plus shift. Thus for the new schedule, caps are [80,40,50,70], which coincide with the original receipt's `limits` (available AC for charging each slot). That's convenient: A gets 80+40, B gets 50+70.\n\nAt 85%, with caps [80,40,50,70], actual acKw = min(request [80,40,50,70], caps)=same. A AC energy = (80+40)*0.5=60 kWh; battery gain = 60*0.85=51 kWh; A end =72+51=123, required 126 -> margin -3. B AC energy=(50+70)*0.5=60; battery gain=51; B end=76+51=127, required 130 -> margin -3. This matches HANDOVER's note: at 85%, with most balanced 20kW shift, A,B each only 123,127, each short 3. Wait HANDOVER says \"即使取最均衡的 20 kW 平移，A、B 各只到 123、127 kWh，各缺 3 kWh\" — yes! That's exactly under [80,40,50,70] caps. And \"正常场景 A 也已缺 3 kWh\" — normal at 85% A=123. So HANDOVER already anticipates the correct limits! It says normal scenario A at 85% is 123 (needs 126) because normal caps [80,40,70,50] gives A 120kW -> 54kWh*0.85=45.9, A=117.9? Wait no. Let's recalc normal at 85% using model: normal caps [80,40,70,50]; A window slots0-1 caps [80,40] => 60 kWh AC *0.85=51, A=123. Yes A window unaffected by slot2/3. So normal A=123 at 85% regardless of caps [80,40,70,50] or [80,40,50,70]. Good. B normal with caps [70,50] =60kWh AC ->51 ->127, short 3. Wait model test says B cold at 85% =130 because normal B needed 54 and min(needed) but test asserted cold B 130? Let's look: test \"85%: ... optimum balance still leaves 3 kWh per bus\" asserts busB cold =130. How? cold caps [80,20,70,50], B window slots2-3 [70,50] =60kWh AC*0.85=51, B=127, not 130. But test says 130. Wait test line 110: close(busB.startKwh + batteryGain(result.cold, busB, 0.85), 130); That seems contradictory. Let me run plan at 0.85 to see. Maybe dispatch caps are computed with efficiency? No, batteryGain function uses scenario.acKw * 0.5 * 0.85. If cold.acKw for B maybe [70,50] -> 60*0.85=51 =>127. Test passes though; maybe cold.acKw B actual is different due to dispatch: A consumes slot1 heavily? Let's run."}
