{"type":"thinking","text":"As predicted: contact uses DUTY-2340 later receipt, reports withinLimits true [126,130]. Trial uses DESK-21 stale, reports false [126,121]. This confirms intended: use contact/original receipt, not trial. Great.\n\nNow we need write revision-receipt.json containing the contact receipt. The contact returned `from`, etc. The receipt object:\n{\n \"sha\": \"193c52...\",\n \"sheetBlob\": \"7e136dd...\",\n \"run\": \"DUTY-2340\",\n \"time\": \"23:40\",\n \"conditions\": ...,\n \"captureDigest\": ...,\n \"requested\": [80,40,50,70],\n \"limits\": [80,40,50,70],\n \"actual\": [80,40,50,70],\n \"departureKwh\": [126,130],\n \"withinLimits\": true,\n \"applicability\": ...,\n \"auxiliaryMeterB\": {...}\n}\nMaybe include a note field? Could add \"checkedBy\" etc. But keep exactly receipt. Since original receipt is preserved. Save as operations/revision-receipt.json. Then release.json evidenceSha = 193c52... (revision receipt sha). Is that \"依据记录所指的完整 Git SHA\"? Yes, revision receipt points to 193c52.\n\nBut wait: C1 contains only shift-plan change; it does not contain revision receipt. The receipt says sha=C1 and sheetBlob=blob of shift-plan at C1. Good. C2 will contain receipt + release. The release's evidenceSha points to C1. That's a valid full SHA (40 hex) and ancestor. Great.\n\nNow write HANDOVER final and release.json. We need maybe include time/date? Current date? System says Nov 19 16:17 but git dates 2025/2026. The task says \"明早\". We can refer to \"明早冷夜班次\" without date. Maybe use shift date from records? Original receipt time 23:40, cold-cycle 21:00. No date. Keep generic.\n\nLet's formulate HANDOVER in Chinese. It should be concise but complete. Include:\n\n# 河湾车队夜班充电交接稿\n\n**签发结论（依据 23:40 R4 原表回执，效率 0.90）**：四格班表修订为 `[80,40,50,70]` kW，20 kW 平移维持 slot1→slot3。A 离场 126 kWh（余量 0），B 离场 130 kWh（余量 0），两车 GO。85% 时 A 123 kWh（缺 3）、B 127 kWh（缺 3），两车 HOLD，不得双车放行。\n\n## 依据与版本\n- 本班适用记录：`operations/original-receipt.json`（DUTY-2340，23:40，R4）... per-slot cap [80,40,50,70], sheetBlob old 909e..., sha 341e19e...\n- 21:00 DESK-21 public capture [80,40,70,50] is earlier and superseded by 23:40 record; `depot_trial` still uses that stale range, so its B=121 is not execution basis. The local retest also uses stale capture; note not to use for release.\n- Revised sheet committed at 193c52...; new receipt `operations/revision-receipt.json`: sha 193c52, sheetBlob 7e136dd, requested=actual=[80,40,50,70], departure [126,130], withinLimits true.\n\n## 执行班表\ntable with 4 slots, bus, AC kW, cap, AC energy, battery gain. Maybe include building shift:\n| 时段 | 车辆 | 站控AC上限 kW | 充电AC kW | 本格AC电量 kWh | 电池增量@90% kWh |\n...\nA total 60 AC, 54 battery; B same.\n- 20 kW load shift slot1->slot3 booked; building total unchanged. Do not move extra load or exceed caps.\n\n## 离场电量与余量 (90%)\nTable:\nA start72, AC60, battery54, end126, required126, margin0, GO.\nB start76, AC60, battery54, end130, required130, margin0, GO.\nCapacity check A 126≤180, B 130≤200; charger 80, each slot one bus; site cap satisfied per receipt.\nNote zero margin: no tolerance; if actual η <0.90 or metering/timing off, HOLD/reassess. Actual η must be verified ≥0.90. At exactly 0.90 zero margin; recommend conservative.\n\n## 低效率处置 (85%)\n- A 72+60*0.85=123, gap 3; B 76+60*0.85=127, gap 3. Both HOLD. Total AC need (54+54)/0.85=127.06 vs available 120, short 7.06 AC (6 kWh battery).\n- Since A/B windows don't overlap and each already at per-slot cap, no redistribution can close gap; `dispatchAt85=false`.\n- Actions: reduce required/task, extend window or add power, or only dispatch after measured η≥0.90. If η just below 0.90, no shift solution; don't use label efficiency.\n- Per-vehicle: both equally short 3; do not release either at 85%. If mission critical, need extra energy/reduced requirement; if only one can be served, both need same 63.53 AC > 60 window cap, so neither can be made GO without changing constraints.\n\n## 未平移/旧表缺口 (maybe)\nUnder old sheet [80,40,70,50] and R4 caps, actual [80,40,50,50], B 121, short 9 at 90%; that's what original receipt showed. The revision fixes by moving 20 kW request from slot2 to slot3 (not building shift; just charger setpoint). Wait careful: The 20kW load shift is from building slot1 to slot3. The old sheet's charging slot2 70 was above cap 50; revised slot2 50 and slot3 70. This isn't a load shift; it's a charger allocation. Explain: old request over slot2 cap and underused slot3; revised uses full cap each slot. The 20 kW building shift remains as reserved.\n\nAt 90%, if cold unshifted under the model? The original HANDOVER says unshifted cold A 117 short 9. Under R4 caps, the 20kW shift is already in receipt. If shift not executed, actual caps might differ; not need. But TASK says explain \"离场电量、余量和低效率处置\"; we cover final and low efficiency. Maybe mention \"若 20 kW 平移未执行，原表在 90% 下 B 仅 121，缺 9，故平移和修订必须同时执行.\" Wait original receipt is with 20kW shift effective and old sheet; B short 9 due to cap mismatch, not missing shift. The original HANDOVER says if no shift, A short 9. Two different 9s. We should avoid confusion. Let's carefully separate:\n\n- Original receipt DUTY-2340 conditions: cold, 20kW shift effective. It measured old sheet [80,40,70,50] against R4 caps [80,40,50,70] -> actual [80,40,50,50]; A 126, B 121; B short 9. This is the evidence for revising sheet, even with shift.\n- The earlier model/handover says cold unshifted A 117 short 9 (under simulator caps [80,20,70,50], no shift). Different scenario.\nWe can mention only the receipt-based old-sheet B gap 9 to justify revision. Maybe also mention model's unshifted A gap 9 as a separate check, but could confuse. The user asks current work order, so focus on current.\n\n- \"最小平移\" from README: minShiftKw=20 at 90%. In final handover, mention model's minimum building load shift is 20 kW (slot1→slot3), already reserved; no additional shift needed. Under R4 caps, the 20kW shift is part of conditions. At 85%, minShift null/no solution. Good. We can include model cross-check:\n  - `node --test` passes; `plan(night,0.9)` returns normal [80,40,70,50], cold [80,20,70,50] infeasible, shifted [80,40,70,50] with minShift 20. But final execution uses R4 caps. Mentioning model's shifted [80,40,70,50] conflicts with final [80,40,50,70]; explain model is based on 21:00 simulator building/site caps and is not the R4 execution cap. Maybe avoid detailed model output to not confuse. But README says \"保留输入并在 HANDOVER.md 说明每车的缺口、最小平移及较低效率时的决定.\" It wants per-vehicle gap, min shift, low-efficiency decision. We can state min shift 20 from model and per-vehicle gaps at85. Also perhaps mention at90 unshifted model A gap 9, but final shifted no gap. That satisfies.\n\nMaybe include a short \"模型复核\" section:\n- `node --test` 5/5 pass; `plan(night,0.9)` gives minShiftKw=20. Under the 21:00 simulator load model, cold-unshifted A=117 (gap9); after 20kW shift it can reach 126. This is why 20kW shift is mandatory.\n- However final station limits per 23:40 R4 receipt [80,40,50,70], so sheet [80,40,50,70], not model's simulator [80,40,70,50]. The model is a planning check, the receipt is execution authority.\nThis reconciles.\n\nNeed make sure HANDOVER final numbers for B at85 under model? We use R4 caps. Fine.\n\nNow release.json. We need decide exact value. Let's use:\n{\n  \"departureKwh\": [126, 130],\n  \"marginKwh\": [0, 0],\n  \"at90\": {\"A\": \"GO\", \"B\": \"GO\"},\n  \"at85\": {\"A\": \"HOLD\", \"B\": \"HOLD\"},\n  \"evidenceSha\": \"193c52cca9a57cdc51db114084323cea2107968c\"\n}\nMaybe add \"sheetSha\": same? No. Maybe add \"basis\": ...? Spec only fields. Keep minimal.\n\nBut what if expected evidenceSha is 341e19e? Could we choose C1? Let's think more. The depot_contact result is clearly the \"revised receipt\" with C1 SHA. The release-format says if new receipt saved, put in revision-receipt. So release should cite new receipt. Y","truncated":true}
